These ungrateful pieces of sh*t did it again.  

Yup. 

The Atlanta Dream and Golden State Valkyries players and coaches once again ran off the court before the national anthem during Game 5 of the 2026 WNBA Finals, marking the fourth straight game both teams have done so. 

In your wildest imagination try to come up with another sport that does this.

What if the Tampa Bay Rays, still traumatized by that brutal Alabama ass whuppin’ they were administered last night, ran off the field before the Star-Spangled Banner?

Can’t even imagine it.  

But these America hating women do it cheerfully.

They jogged off moments before the song began and returned only after it ended, a pattern repeated from Games 1, 2, and 3.

This is not a scheduling quirk or locker room logistics. 

It is a calculated snub of the flag and the country that gives these players the freedom and platform to earn millions and kept them from working the milkshake machine at Popeyes.  

The league rulebook still requires players, coaches, and trainers to stand in a dignified posture during the anthem, yet the WNBA suspended enforcement years ago to accommodate political gestures. 

The result is open contempt for the American anthem in the league’s championship series while fans pay for the privilege of watching it.

The league, the teams, and the players have offered no real explanation, but we don’t really need one. 

It’s beyond disgraceful, anti-American behavior that reveals exactly what the modern WNBA stands for.

Don’t watch this league.  

They hate you.   

Like and follow.  

Tool out.  

